            <div type="translation" source="bib:Kuppusamy+al2010_01">
                <p n="1">Hail! Prosperity!</p>
                <p n="1">Year 22 <supplied reason="subaudible">of the reign</supplied> of Kaṉṉara-tēvar.</p>
                <p n="2-5">The donation that we, the shepherds of Vākūr-nāṭu on the Northern bank of Vēcālippāṭi set up for the Lord of śrī-Mūlastāṉam of Vākūr <supplied reason="subaudible">is as follows</supplied>.</p>
                <p n="5-6">At the occasion of climbing the cot<note>A ritual during the marriage.</note> we shall give a sheep <supplied reason="subaudible">to the temple on behalf of the shepherd</supplied> and climb the cot.</p>
                <p n="6-9">We shall give a sheep to the shepherd who migrates from other country and climbs the cot in this <foreign>nāṭu</foreign>.</p>
                <p n="10-12">If we violate <supplied reason="subaudible">this prescription</supplied>, the important members of the <supplied reason="subaudible">village administrative</supplied> group and the temple servants <supplied reason="subaudible">ancers</supplied> shall seize two <supplied reason="subaudible">of our</supplied> sheep.</p>
                <p n="12-13">We, the shepherds of this <foreign>nāṭu</foreign>, have <supplied reason="subaudible">thus</supplied> ordained upon mutual consent.</p>
                <p n="13-16">We, who do the work of the sluice <foreign>mataku</foreign><note>That is, sluice openers.</note> of this <foreign>nāṭu</foreign>, shall maintain this donation so that it exists as long as the moon and the sun will last.</p>
                <p n="16">Prosperity.</p>
            </div>
            
